tion/pre-write so a sweep failure leaves the prior view intact; receipt embeds the sweep outcome.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\", \"reason\": \"CompactReceipt.sweep flipped from SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} | \\\"absent\\\" to SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} — Story 2's debt comment closed.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: assertSweepReceiptShape — the single structural validator both the Story 3 SDK leg and Story 5's spawned CLI parity leg assert against (TC-3.3's shared-schema mechanism).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"Re-exports assertSweepReceiptShape and the classification table (REASON_CLASS_TABLE/classifyFailureReason) — fixtures are the boundary-exempt bridge for the story-sanctioned exported-for-tests table.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: 10 tests covering TC-3.1–3.4, the classification-edge architecture-risk legs (blocked never requeued, structural noop dedupe via a turn pair sharing one work item, unclassified-permanent through the production terminal write path), the table unit legs, and the zero-provider assertion completed across all five thread-view ops.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: sweep is real now, so its not-implemented stub leg moved out; materialize keeps the stub assertion until Story 5.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: receipt assertion flipped from sweep:\\\"absent\\\" to the embedded SweepReceipt, asserting the file's first default compact requeues the fixture's transient failure (which keeps the later record-untouched assertions honest).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Re-recorded hashes for the two sanctioned amendments (record-red-manifest.mjs), keeping the test-immutability gate