{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01BNe5xGxh6NMKqc74qv4Pih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Self-review pass 2: requirement alignment, test coverage, and missing evidence. Walked every obligation in the story/tech-design/test-plan handoff against implemented evidence. AC-3.1 (owners' surfaces only): verified structurally — sweep.ts imports only type vocabulary plus messages/turns index surfaces, zero sqlite/openThreadDatabase/work_item/derived_form touches; behaviorally pinned by the five-op zero-provider test and the work-row read-backs through openRaw. AC-3.2: TC-3.1's elapsed bound plus an anti-shim grep (no drainSettled/polling in sweep.ts or the surface). AC-3.3: TC-3.1 covers all five seeded states — blocked lives on the sacrificial sibling thread per the design's own fixture spec (FC-0.3 puts blocked source-damage on a sibling), so the blocked leg is a sibling sweep, design-conformant. AC-3.4: TC-3.2 plus the structural owner-noop leg (turn pair sharing one work item). AC-3.5: receipt lines asserted per owner/kind with reasons for failed and blocked. AC-3.6: TC-3.4 skip + default-embed + heal legs, with the heal riding the background scheduler via the requeue's poke-on-commit and the healed form proven in the served view (boundary-seeded pull renders the ready summary). AC-3.7: standalone-vs-embedded same shape holds by construction (both call sites share runSweep — verified) and the shared schema validator passes both; the CLI execution leg is the story's own explicit Scope-out to Story 5. Classification table is data with the unclassified-permanent default tested at unit, production-write-path, and receipt levels. Gate-before-first-commit obligation satisfied (recorded in the team-impl-log; nothing committed yet). One evidence gap found and fixed this pass: view-sweep.test.ts was not recorded in the red-manifest, so the test-immutability gate would not have covered it going forward — recorded (37 files now) and green-verify re-run clean.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: reason-code classification table as data (unclassified ⇒ permanent), report walk over both owners, bucket ready/in-flight/blocked/failed×classify, transient requeue through owners' surfaces with already_queued noop counted in-flight, per-owner/kind receipt assembly. No waiting, no provider calls, no direct work_item/derived_form writes (verified structurally this pass).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"sweep surface op real (stub removed); compact gains the default-on sweep step with sweep:false skip, post-validation/pre-write so a sweep failure leaves the prior view intact; standalone and embedded paths share runSweep, making AC-3.7's same-receipt-shape structural.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\", \"reason\": \"CompactReceipt.sweep flipped from SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} | \\\"absent\\\" to SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} — Story 2's debt comment closed.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: assertSweepReceiptShape — the single structural validator both the Story 3 SDK leg and Story 5's spawned CLI parity leg assert against (TC-3.3's shared-schema mechanism).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"Re-exports assertSweepReceiptShape and the classification table (REASON_CLASS_TABLE/classifyFailureReason) — fixtures are the boundary-exempt bridge for the story-sanctioned exported-for-tests table.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: 10 tests covering TC-3.1–3.4, the classification-edge architecture-risk legs (blocked never requeued, structural noop dedupe, unclassified-permanent via the production terminal write path), the table unit legs, and the zero-provider assertion completed across all five thread-view ops.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: sweep is real now, so its not-implemented stub leg moved out; materialize keeps the stub assertion until Story 5.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: receipt assertion flipped from sweep:\\\"absent\\\" to the embedded SweepReceipt, asserting the file's first default compact requeues the fixture's transient failure.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Re-recorded hashes for the two sanctioned amendments; pass 2 additionally recorded view-sweep.test.ts so the immutability gate covers the new suite going forward (37 files).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md\", \"reason\": \"Phase updated to implement COMPLETE with recovery detail, SV-03-001/002 closure evidence, gate results, and the retained verifier handle for the follow-up verify.\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.1: buckets the five seeded states, requeues only the transient failure, returns without waiting, zero provider calls\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.2 (AC-3.4): a second sweep without draining reports the requeued form in-flight and writes no second row\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.3 schema leg (AC-3.5, AC-3.7): the SDK receipt validates against the shared receipt schema\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: zero-provider assertion across all five ops (architecture-risk)\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: blocked forms are reported with their stored reasons and never requeued\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: once-per-invocation dedupe is structural: a turn's two transiently-failed forms share one work row, the second ask noops to in-flight\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: an unclassified reason code lands in permanentFailed with its literal reason and is never requeued\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: the classification table is data: named classes map as designed, everything else is permanent\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: compact with sweep: false records the skip and requeues nothing\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: default compact embeds the sweep receipt; the drained requeue heals into the next compact's view\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"test/view-pull.test.ts :: surface skeleton stub leg (sweep removed from the not-implemented set; materialize-only now)\",\n      \"test/view-compact.test.ts :: compacts with a built-in profile (sweep:\\\"absent\\\" assertion replaced with embedded-receipt + requeue assertion)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 273,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 10\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"Pass 2: view-sweep.test.ts was missing from test/red-manifest.json, so the test-immutability gate would not have protected the new suite after this story closes (prior stories recorded their new test files). Recorded via scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs (manifest now 37 files); green-verify re-run clean (273 tests, immutability OK).\",\n      \"Pass 1 (carried): TC-3.4 heal leg rewritten from a touch-suppressed background status call to a background-SDK compact whose requeue poke-on-commit drives the production repair path.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"AC-3.7's CLI execution leg is deferred to Story 5's process suite by the story's own Scope-out; the shared receipt-schema validator landed here so the Story 5 leg asserts the same checker — verifier should confirm this deferral reading.\",\n      \"TC-3.1's blocked state is asserted on the sacrificial sibling thread rather than the main fixture thread — this follows the design's own fixture specification (blocked source-damage lives on a sibling, FC-0.3/test-plan §Test Substrate), not a coverage shortcut.\",\n      \"Untested edge (schema-valid, outside the plan's TC set): sweep on a thread with no derived forms returns an empty-owners receipt; no test pins it.\",\n      \"If an owner requeue fails mid-walk, sweep returns the error and that invocation's receipt is lost; already-committed requeues are durable (each is its own owner transaction) and surface as in-flight on the next sweep. Receipt-level partial-failure accounting was not specified.\",\n      \"Default-on sweep means compact now legitimately mutates derivation state on a thread with transient failures; view-compact.test.ts's record-untouched assertions depend on the file's first default compact performing the one requeue — order coupling documented in the amended test comment.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Run the story-verify follow-up on the retained verifier handle (codex/019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6) against SV-03-001/SV-03-002 closure, then the story receipt/commit. CLI parity leg for sweep (TC-3.3 execution half) lands in Story 5's process suite as planned.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_read_input_tokens":185689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14af1c76-5e3a-4e59-acc7-c3c9d062b23f","uuid":"3c8a8055-2df7-4424-b320-028c6361d96c","request_id":"req_011CbwrinuJUh1GmSouomV3E"}
