{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01UWEEC4S8BweJ2AoMqueynA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Self-review pass 3: residual risks, scope edges, and pre-handoff fixes. Placeholder scan over all changed files found nothing unintended — the only remaining stub is materialize (Story 5's by design, with its structured-result contract intact) and historical comments. Production-path gap scan: none found — the sweep's owner dispatch handles both subject vocabularies correctly (messages by messageId, turns by turn|chunk), receipt line order is deterministic (owners' report ORDER BY through Map insertion order, which Story 5's CLI parity comparison will rely on), and the compact embed shares the standalone walk. Re-ran verify-all after pass 2's manifest addition since the prior epic-gate run predated it: 300 tests pass. Reconciled the test-count convention against the log's own Cumulative Baselines section (which pins verify-all counts: baseline 290, expected ~300): actual is exactly 300, so this payload's totals now follow the log's convention (totalAfterStory 300, delta +10; default suite 273) and the log's Latest Actual Total was updated from 290 to 300 — this also resolves the log's lesson-5 baseline-definition ambiguity for this story by deferring to the log's stated definition. Handoff obligations checked against the log structure: the Story 3 receipt section (## Story Receipts) and Current Continuation Handles entries are written at the receipt step after the verify follow-up, not by the implementor — called out as the explicit remaining handoff work. Two design-accepted residual risks restated for the verifier rather than silently carried.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: reason-code classification table as data (unclassified ⇒ permanent), report walk over both owners, bucket ready/in-flight/blocked/failed×classify, transient requeue through owners' surfaces with already_queued noop counted in-flight, per-owner/kind receipt assembly. No waiting, no provider calls, no direct work_item/derived_form writes (verified structurally in pass 2).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"sweep surface op real (stub removed); compact gains the default-on sweep step with sweep:false skip, post-validation/pre-write so a sweep failure leaves the prior view intact; standalone and embedded paths share runSweep, making AC-3.7's same-receipt-shape structural.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\", \"reason\": \"CompactReceipt.sweep flipped from SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} | \\\"absent\\\" to SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} — Story 2's debt comment closed.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: assertSweepReceiptShape — the single structural validator both the Story 3 SDK leg and Story 5's spawned CLI parity leg assert against (TC-3.3's shared-schema mechanism).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"Re-exports assertSweepReceiptShape and the classification table (REASON_CLASS_TABLE/classifyFailureReason) — fixtures are the boundary-exempt bridge for the story-sanctioned exported-for-tests table.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"New: 10 tests covering TC-3.1–3.4, the classification-edge architecture-risk legs (blocked never requeued, structural noop dedupe, unclassified-permanent via the production terminal write path), the table unit legs, and the zero-provider assertion completed across all five thread-view ops.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: sweep is real now, so its not-implemented stub leg moved out; materialize keeps the stub assertion until Story 5.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Sanctioned amendment: receipt assertion flipped from sweep:\\\"absent\\\" to the embedded SweepReceipt, asserting the file's first default compact requeues the fixture's transient failure.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Re-recorded hashes for the two sanctioned amendments; view-sweep.test.ts recorded (pass 2) so the immutability gate covers the new suite going forward (37 files).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md\", \"reason\": \"Phase updated to implement COMPLETE with recovery detail, SV-03-001/002 closure evidence, gate results, retained verifier handle; pass 3 updated Cumulative Baselines' Latest Actual Total to 300 per the log's verify-all counting convention.\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.1: buckets the five seeded states, requeues only the transient failure, returns without waiting, zero provider calls\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.2 (AC-3.4): a second sweep without draining reports the requeued form in-flight and writes no second row\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.3 schema leg (AC-3.5, AC-3.7): the SDK receipt validates against the shared receipt schema\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: zero-provider assertion across all five ops (architecture-risk)\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: blocked forms are reported with their stored reasons and never requeued\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: once-per-invocation dedupe is structural: a turn's two transiently-failed forms share one work row, the second ask noops to in-flight\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: an unclassified reason code lands in permanentFailed with its literal reason and is never requeued\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: the classification table is data: named classes map as designed, everything else is permanent\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: compact with sweep: false records the skip and requeues nothing\",\n      \"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: default compact embeds the sweep receipt; the drained requeue heals into the next compact's view\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"test/view-pull.test.ts :: surface skeleton stub leg (sweep removed from the not-implemented set; materialize-only now)\",\n      \"test/view-compact.test.ts :: compacts with a built-in profile (sweep:\\\"absent\\\" assertion replaced with embedded-receipt + requeue assertion)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 300,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 10\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"Pass 3: test-count reporting reconciled to the log's own Cumulative Baselines convention (verify-all counts) — totalAfterStory is 300 against the recorded 290 baseline, exactly the +10 estimate; the log's Latest Actual Total updated 290→300. verify-all re-run after pass 2's manifest change: 300 pass.\",\n      \"Pass 2 (carried): view-sweep.test.ts recorded into the red-manifest so the immutability gate protects the new suite (37 files).\",\n      \"Pass 1 (carried): TC-3.4 heal leg rewritten to drive the drain through a background-SDK compact's requeue poke-on-commit (the production path) instead of a touch-suppressed status call.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Handoff obligation remaining (next step, not implementor's): the team-impl-log's ## Story Receipts section needs the 03-readiness-sweep receipt entry and Current Continuation Handles needs the verifier-handle update at the receipt step after the verify follow-up.\",\n      \"Design-accepted residual risk (Deferred Items, restated): there is no cross-invocation requeue cap — a failure that persists a transient-class code but never heals re-requeues at every compact, spending one provider attempt cycle each time; receipt visibility is the v1 mitigation.\",\n      \"If an owner requeue fails mid-walk, sweep returns the error and that invocation's receipt is lost; committed requeues are durable and surface as in-flight on the next sweep — partial-failure receipt accounting was not specified.\",\n      \"AC-3.7's CLI execution leg is the story's explicit Scope-out to Story 5's process suite; the shared receipt-schema validator landed here for that leg to assert against.\",\n      \"Untested edge (schema-valid, outside the plan's TC set): sweep on a thread with no derived forms returns an empty-owners receipt.\",\n      \"view-compact.test.ts's record-untouched assertions depend on the file's first default compact performing the fixture's one transient requeue — order coupling documented in the amended test comment.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Run the story-verify follow-up on the retained verifier handle (codex/019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6) against SV-03-001/SV-03-002 closure, then write the Story 3 receipt into the team-impl-log and commit. CLI parity leg for sweep (TC-3.3 execution half) lands in Story 5's process suite as planned.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":660,"cache_read_input_tokens":195059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":660},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14af1c76-5e3a-4e59-acc7-c3c9d062b23f","uuid":"e7c6e5fe-cb90-4035-bc4a-47c5962a6621","request_id":"req_011CbwrrnNmsiP83nhgxJri1"}
